# Adding tests to sales_toolkit

When asked to add tests for a function:

1. Read the function and its docstring. List the business rules it must obey.
2. Before writing any test, write a short table in your reply:
   | case | input | expected output | why this case matters |
   Include at least: one normal case, one boundary (for example 0 or 100
   percent), and one invalid input.
3. Compute every expected value by hand from the business rules. Never
   compute an expected value by calling the function under test.
4. Put the tests in `tests/test_<module>.py`, one behaviour per test, with a
   descriptive name such as `test_discount_of_100_percent_gives_zero`.
5. Use `Decimal("...")` strings for money, never floats.
6. Run `python -m pytest -q` and report exactly which tests pass and fail.
7. Do NOT change code in `sales_toolkit/` in this task. If a test fails,
   report it as a possible defect and stop.
